## 4. 🔐 PERMISSIONS & SYSTEM ACCESS ARCHITECTURE

### 4.1 The "777" Reality on Android
Android does not have a Unix-style chmod 777 for apps. Filesystem access is a layered system of manifest permissions, special app access grants (Settings pages), and privileged escalation (ADB/Shizuku/Root). The app must request all three layers to achieve maximum practical access.

### 4.2 Storage Access (All Files & Folders)

| Permission | Type | What It Grants | How to Grant |
|---|---|---|---|
| MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE | Special app access (Settings) | Read/write all files in shared storage (internal + SD card + OTG), including /sdcard/Android/ subdirs (except other apps' private dirs) | Manifest declaration + ACTION_MANAGE_ALL_FILES_ACCESS_PERMISSION intent to system Settings |
| READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE | Runtime (≤ API 32) | Legacy read access to shared storage | Runtime dialog (older devices) |
| WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE | Runtime (≤ API 29) | Legacy write access to shared storage | Runtime dialog (older devices) |
| READ_MEDIA_IMAGES | Runtime (API 33+) | Read images from shared storage | Runtime dialog (granular media permission) |

ADB grant command for full storage:
adb shell appops set --uid <PACKAGE_NAME> MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE allow

What MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE still cannot access: other apps' private data directories (/data/data/<other_app>) and their app-specific external dirs (/sdcard/Android/data/<other_app>). Those require Shizuku or Root.

### 4.3 Special App Access (Settings-Granted Permissions)

| Permission | Purpose | How to Grant |
|---|---|---|
| SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW | Draw overlays on top of other apps (floating UI, ESP overlays, agent status HUD) | System Settings page (ACTION_MANAGE_OVERLAY_PERMISSION); cannot be granted via runtime dialog |
| REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES | Install APKs from within the app (rebuild → sign → install pipeline) | Manifest + per-source user approval (Android 8.0+) |
| WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS | Modify system settings (auto-enable wireless debugging, toggle accessibility services) | adb shell pm grant <PACKAGE_NAME> android.permission.WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS |
| PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS | Read app usage statistics (monitor target games) | Settings → Special app access → Usage access |
| ACCESS_NOTIFICATION_POLICY | Control Do Not Disturb (silent background builds) | Manifest + Settings grant (optional) |

### 4.4 Background Execution & Persistence

| Permission | Purpose |
|---|---|
| FOREGROUND_SERVICE | Required for long-lived background tasks (builds, indexing, agent loops) |
| FOREGROUND_SERVICE_SPECIAL_USE | Declare a specialized foreground service type for the agent (API 34+) |
| FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC | Background file indexing and sync operations |
| POST_NOTIFICATIONS | Foreground service notifications and agent approval prompts (API 33+) |
| RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED | Auto-start agent service after reboot (restore scheduled routines, watchers) |
| WAKE_LOCK | Keep CPU awake during long builds, downloads, instrumentation sessions |
| SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM | Precise timing for scheduled routines |

### 4.5 Package & App Visibility

| Permission | Purpose | When Needed |
|---|---|---|
| QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES | Query all installed apps (detect CODM/MLBB by package name, enumerate modding targets) | Essential for game profile auto-detection. Alternative: <queries> intent filters targeting known game packages to avoid the broad permission |

### 4.6 Network & Connectivity

| Permission | Purpose |
|---|---|
| INTERNET | Gemini API calls, web search, URL context, dependency audit |
| ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE | Detect network availability before API calls |
| ACCESS_WIFI_STATE | Detect WiFi for ADB-over-WiFi pairing (optional) |

### 4.7 Accessibility Service (Computer Use / Screen Automation)
Allows reading screen content of any app and injecting gestures — used for testing mods, navigating game UIs, or Computer Use.

| Service Attribute | Purpose |
|---|---|
| canRetrieveWindowContent | Read view hierarchy of any app on screen |
| canPerformGestures | Simulate taps, swipes, long-presses in other apps |
| canTakeScreenshot | Capture screenshots of the current screen |
| accessibilityEventTypes="typeAllMask" | Receive all accessibility events from all apps |

Declaration: AndroidManifest.xml → <service android:name=".AgentAccessibilityService" android:permission="android.permission.BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE"> with accessibility-service.xml config.

### 4.8 Privileged Escalation Paths (Beyond Manifest Permissions)

| Path | Access Level | How to Enable | What It Unlocks |
|---|---|---|---|
| ADB (appops) | Shell (UID 2000) | adb shell appops set ... commands | MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE, WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS, package installation, shell commands |
| Shizuku | Shell (UID 2000) | Install Shizuku app → start via ADB or root → grant moe.shizuku.manager.permission.API_V23 | Full shell access, app_process APIs, install/uninstall, settings manipulation, /data/local/tmp access |
| Root (libsu) | UID 0 | Device must be rooted (Magisk/KernelSU/APatch) | Full /data/, /system/, other apps' private dirs, kernel-level operations |

Shizuku integration permissions to declare:
- moe.shizuku.manager.permission.API_V23 — runtime permission for Shizuku binder access
- Shizuku provider declaration in AndroidManifest.xml

