### 4.10 First-Run Permission Request Flow
1. Storage first — request MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE via Settings intent; show ADB fallback command
2. Shizuku/Root detection — check if Shizuku binder is available; if not, offer ADB setup instructions
3. Notifications — request POST_NOTIFICATIONS (API 33+)
4. Overlay — request SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW (only if floating UI/ESP features are used)
5. Install permission — request REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES (only when first APK install is attempted)
6. Accessibility — request only when Computer Use or screen automation is first triggered
7. Battery optimization exemption — REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS for long-running background agents

### 4.11 What Each Tier Unlocks for CODM/MLBB

| Capability | SAF only | + MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE | + Shizuku | + Root |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Read APK from /sdcard | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Write to /sdcard/Android/data/ | ❌ | ❌ (blocked) | ✅ | ✅ |
| Read /data/local/tmp | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Read other apps' /data/data/ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |
| Install APK silently | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ (Shizuku) | ✅ |
| Dump memory of running game | ❌ | ❌ | ⚠️ (process attach may still be blocked) | ✅ (ptrace) |
| Modify /system/ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |

