## 5. 🛠️ TOOL SET (GEMINI FUNCTION CALLING)

Read tools:
- list_directory, read_file, glob_files, grep / ripgrep, read_bytes(path, offset, len)

Large file tools:
- file_stat(path) → size, line_count (streamed), sha256 (streamed), mime — no full load
- read_lines(path, start, end) → line range for text files
- grep_large(path, pattern, context_lines) → ripgrep-backed; returns byte offsets + snippets
- read_bytes(path, offset, len) → binary window (max 1 MB per call)
- index_file(path) → build SQLite FTS5 index locally
- search_index(query, path_prefix) → search indexed files without loading
- tail_file(path, n) → last N lines (logcat-style)
- pipe_to_shell(path, shell_cmd) → stream file through strings/grep/awk without loading into context

Write tools (all approval-gated by default):
- write_file, edit_file, delete_file (→ trash), create_folder, patch_bytes, move_file, copy_file

Execution tools:
- run_shell_command (Termux RUN_COMMAND intent, runs in workspace cwd)
- tail_logcat(package), install_apk, uninstall_app
- background_start / background_status / background_kill (long-running processes)

Domain tools:
- git_status / diff / log / commit / stash / branch
- apk_decompile / apk_build / apk_sign / apk_install
- jadx_decompile, read_smali_class, find_method, xref
- zip_list, zip_read_entry, zip_patch_entry (respects resources.arsc stored-not-deflated rule)
- arsc_decode, binary_xml_decode, nine_patch_decode
- frida_run(script), memory_search(pattern)
- web_search (Google Search grounding), fetch_url (URL context)
- code_exec (sandboxed Python for computation)
- scan_vulnerabilities, audit_dependencies
- generate_image (Nano Banana / Imagen)

API-level features to use:
- Parallel function calling with stable UUIDs
- Streaming function-call arguments (streamFunctionCallArguments) for progress UI
- JSON Schema tool definitions (portable)
- Context caching for large repeated workspaces

