## 15. ⚠️ REALISTIC WARNINGS

- The phased order above is deliberate — each phase is independently useful, so the app is usable before it is complete.
- Large file infrastructure is Phase 2, not a later addition — CODM and MLBB assets routinely exceed 100 MB, and retrofitting memory-mapped reads + FTS5 indexing after the write tools ship is expensive.
- Phase 3 (diffs + undo) is non-negotiable before any write tool ships. Shipping writes without undo will cost you a project.
- Skip shell until Phase 4 — rm -rf from a misread prompt is the #1 way this app destroys your work.
- Termux must be installed and its RUN_COMMAND intent permission configured for the shell tool.
- Root is optional — Shizuku + adb grant covers 80% of modding needs, but true /data/data/ access and silent installs at full capability require root or Shizuku.
- MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE does not grant access to /sdcard/Android/data/ — Shizuku or root is required for that path.
- Gemini 4 Argon context is 1,048,576 tokens unified (input + output + thinking + function calls) — the HUD and compaction are essential, not cosmetic.
- Never attempt a full-context read of any file > 5 MB — the token math makes it impossible and the app must refuse rather than truncate silently.
- Accessibility service is the highest-risk permission surface — gate it behind an explicit toggle and never enable it silently.
- QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES is a broad permission; if you want to minimize it, use <queries> intent filters for known game packages instead.